cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project or its code, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Coolant: Predictive Machine Learning for HPC Thermal Management"
abstract: >
  A machine learning framework that forecasts coolant return temperature and
  classifies thermal risk 10 minutes ahead using real telemetry from Frontier,
  the exascale supercomputer at Oak Ridge National Laboratory. Inspired by
  Jadhav & Liu (2026), IEEE ITherm Best Paper, this project extends that work
  with a predictive forecasting and risk-classification layer for proactive
  cooling control.

